    "title": "Columbia County aims to eliminate homestead property taxes by 2029 - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Sydney Palmer ,\n7 hours ago\nCOLUMBIA COUNTY, Ga. (WRDW/WAGT) - Columbia County plans to use excess revenue, including money from the new Google data center, to pay property taxes for homeowners with a homestead exemption, County Manager Scott Johnson said. Johnson said full elimination of homestead property taxes depends on a state constitutional amendment that...\nRead full article\nAdd to Preferred Sources\n4",
